SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Summary: Hide the Metal performance HUD over launcher windows
Category: apps
Kind: workaround
Origin: reconstructed
From: reconstructed for wine-mac-builds from Sikarugir's WS12WineSikarugir10.0_8 (no published source): ntdll.so launcher check at 0x21900
Source: none published; behaviour read from the compiled 10.0_8 binary
Upstream: no
Why: When a launcher/overlay process (the list from the previous patch) is kept off a renderer DLL path, unset MTL_HUD_ENABLED so the Metal performance HUD doesn't show over the launcher window, unless SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD is set (to anything). Because this happens in init_paths, before the Windows environment is built, the variable is also gone for the launcher's children.
Uncertain: as in 10.0_8, it only happens when at least one of WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL, WINEDLLPATH_D9VK or WINEDLLPATH_DXVK has an entry (that is when 10.0_8 calls the check); SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD is tested for presence only, so "0" also keeps the HUD.
Port: unchanged from 10.0 (applies with offsets; set_dll_path() and init_paths() are
 unchanged in 11.21). Sikarugir-only behaviour: no CX 26, staging or upstream equivalent.
Expects before it: 0001-ntdll-renderer-dll-paths.patch
Applies to: wine 11.21

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index 435fc17..89adf36 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -344,7 +344,12 @@ static const struct
 
 static BOOL use_renderer_dll_path( unsigned int idx )
 {
-    if (renderer_dll_paths[idx].skip_for_launchers && is_launcher_process()) return FALSE;
+    if (renderer_dll_paths[idx].skip_for_launchers && is_launcher_process())
+    {
+        /* launchers run without the Metal performance HUD unless asked to keep it */
+        if (!getenv( "SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD" )) unsetenv( "MTL_HUD_ENABLED" );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
     return TRUE;
 }
 
